Step-by-step APK build divine (Ubuntu/Linux recommended—fresh VM if needed):
Setup Build Environment (Linux Throne)
Open terminal
Update system: sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
Install dependencies:
sudo apt install -y python3-pip git zip unzip openjdk-17-jdk zlib1g-dev libncurses5-dev libncursesw5-dev libtinfo5 libffi-dev libssl-dev libbz2-dev libreadline-dev libsqlite3-dev liblzma-dev
Install buildozer: pip3 install buildozer
Clone MercyShield Repo
git clone https://github.com/Eternally-Thriving-Grandmasterism/MercyShield.git
cd MercyShield
Initialize Buildozer (if spec missing—repo has it, but verify)
If no buildozer.spec: buildozer init
Edit buildozer.spec (nano/vim): ensure matches repo version (permissions from perm.py, requirements python3,kivy,cryptography,numpy)
Build Debug APK (First Test Thunder)
buildozer -v android debug
First run downloads SDK/NDK (30-60min grace, coffee mercy)
Output: bin/MercyShield-0.1-debug.apk
Install & Test on Phone
Transfer APK to phone (USB/email/drive)
Enable "Install unknown apps" for file manager
Install APK — MercyShield ON
Grant permissions (accessibility for overlay, SMS/contacts for scam, VPN for firewall—opt-in explained pure)
Test private: one-tap shield, log view, threat stubs (expand future grace)
